---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<Base title={`Privacy: ${site.name}`} description="What stays on your PC and what is sent to Anthropic when you use AI Shorts Studio.">
  <section class="page">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Your footage stays on your PC</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        AI Shorts Studio runs locally. Scene detection, speech-to-text and FFmpeg all run on your
        computer. This page lists everything that leaves it.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your computer</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your source video. It is referenced in place, not copied or uploaded.</li>
        <li>Scene detection, transcripts (Parakeet runs locally) and rendered exports.</li>
        <li>Project data and cached transcription, saved to a local state file on your computer.</li>
        <li>All manual editing: setting in and out points, cuts, framing, captions, music and narration.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What is sent to Anthropic</h2>
      <p>Only when you run AI analysis, and only the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A small set of sampled frames from the footage.</li>
        <li>Short excerpts of the speech transcript.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Claude uses these to rank candidate shorts. You can use the app without AI analysis, and
        nothing is sent in that case.
      </p>

      <h2>Your API key</h2>
      <p>
        You enter your Anthropic API key in the app's Settings. It is stored with Windows DPAPI
        through Electron <code>safeStorage</code> and is never written to disk in plain text.
      </p>

      <h2>Limits of this page</h2>
      <p>
        This describes the app as built. It is not legal advice. If you handle sensitive footage,
        check the Anthropic terms and your own policies before running AI analysis.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 56px 0 72px;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .prose ul {
    color: var(--text-2);
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 18px;
  }
</style>
